 "customerTurns": 4,
 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "microwve plate wont go round anymore, food hot on one side cold on other. still heats tho"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is tray seated correctly / obstruction. Can you tell me whether tray not sitting on the coupler/rollers properly?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "the plate sits on the middle bit but it wobbles a bit. dropped it in the sink last week and put it back on a bit roughly if that matters"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Lift the glass tray out. Check the small three-pronged coupler in the middle isn't cracked, clean the roller ring and the floor under it, then refit the tray so its grooves sit on the coupler — and make sure a large dish isn't catching the sides. Was the tray off the coupler, dirty or catching (and is it sorted), is the coupler or roller ring broken, or did it all look fine?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok had a look, the little plastic three-pronged bit in the middle has a crack in it and the hole in the middle looks all rounded. roller ring is in place and the wheels spin fine, nothing stuck under it"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: turntable coupler]\nThe checks point to the turntable coupler. To find the right part, could you give me the make and model number? It is usually on the back or inside the door frame.\n[Panel: \"To check a suitable replacement — Enter your model number below. Once we have the model I can check whether a suitable replacement is available. It's usually on a sticker inside the door or around the frame, or on the back of the appliance.\"]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "its a Sharp, model R272WM, found it on the label at the back"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: turntable coupler]\nThe checks point to the turntable coupler. I could not find a confirmed match for model R272WM in our parts catalogue, so check with the manufacturer or a parts supplier using the full model number, or ask an appliance engineer to fit it."
  }
 ],
